Z||000018||87FieroGT||12-10-1999||11:47 PM||||To Carrolles,<BR>     The front license plate is required but I have never been pulled over for it. And besides if a "corvette" owner doesn't have to have one on the front of his car why should a FIERO owner have to have one? Besides it looks better without the plate there.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Standard||12-10-1999||11:57 PM||||I think it's required to have one on the front here in Minnesota too, but I had a bra on <B>my car</B> for about 3 months that covered the plate (didn't feel like cutting out the hole), and I never go pulled over for it, either.<P>just wanted to make sure that somebody didn't misread that... lol!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 12-10-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||12:12 AM||||My wifes car is registered in Ohio.  (OH is another one of those paranoid states that makes you have 2 plates.)  We live in Indiana (very long story).  I took the front plate off of her car.  We go back to OH about once a month and haven't been stopped yet.<P>87FieroGT-Corvette owners have to have front plates in the dumb states, too.  All cars have to have a provision for a front plate.  Some of them look better than others, though.  I think that the front plate holder/hanger is some kind of option for a Corvette.  At least the C5s.  I'll check tomorrow.  I certainly have the time.||||reg||1
Z||000021||fiero56||12-11-1999||08:31 AM||||I had the front plates on my Fiero for about a month, then decided I didn't want the front one on anymore.  Been driving without it since about April, no problems yet. I have a friend who was pulled over for not having one in front, but that was several years ago.||||reg||7
Z||000022||87GTBro||12-14-1999||08:57 PM||||I think we get away with not having a front plate because most policemen don't feel like messing with the issue.  A real rookie officer who goes strictly by the book might pull you over, but the average officer doesn't feel like enforcing it.<P>I think all Fieros look better without the front plate.  I'm taking mine off as soon as I buy my 86.5 GT in the morning...||||reg||1
Z||000023||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||09:49 PM||||Kinda like turn signals.  It's a law (and, IMHO, should be), but bears don't mess with you if you don't use them (wish they would!).||||reg||1
